<title>CANADA: Wal-Mart Canada plans 6 new stores.</title>
<headline>Wal-Mart Canada plans 6 new stores.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wal-Mart Canada Inc, a unit of Wal-Mart Stores Inc, said on Wednesday that it would open six stores in Canada in 1997 and 1998 to bring its total to 142 outlets from 136.</p>
<p>Wal-Mart Canada, which has become Canada's largest discount department chain since its arrival in 1994, said it would open stores in Ontario, Quebec and Alberta and employ 600 more workers.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
</text>
